        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the most common Ketogenics complaints?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most complaints concern buying rather than the powder. KetoGenics isn't on Amazon, so orders carry shipping costs and take longer. Some buyers find stevia-only Zero Carb milder than artificially sweetened shakes, which the brand itself acknowledges. Zero Carb's 22 g of protein per scoop is also a few grams lower than most isolates. The brand's own reviews average about 4.95 stars."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I buy Ketogenics protein powder on Amazon?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not from the brand, as far as we could find on November 21, 2026. Our Amazon searches returned no KetoGenics protein listings, and the brand sells through its own store at KetoShop.com, where both proteins were $49.99. The closest Amazon alternative is Isopure Zero Carb, which also lists 0 g of carbs and 25 g of protein per scoop but uses sucralose."
          }
        }
